  "body": "First time is on the market in 28 years.\r\n\r\nSometimes the best opportunities in Orakei come wrapped in plaster.\r\n\r\nHeld by the same owners since day one, this freehold, north-facing property is tucked away down a private driveway behind electric gates - and it's finally looking for its next chapter.\r\n\r\nFour bedrooms, three bathrooms, double garaging, a new kitchen, new flooring upstairs and a huge enclosed all-year-round deck.\r\n\r\nSounds good, right?\r\n\r\nWell... we're not going to pretend it doesn't come with a bit of homework.\r\n\r\nThe house is plaster, it does not have a CCC and it is being sold \"As Is, Where Is\".\r\n\r\nStill reading? Good. Because this is where it gets interesting.\r\n\r\nThe bones of a seriously exciting property are already here. You've got space, privacy, garaging and improvements already made - but the real superstar is the position.\r\n\r\nUninterrupted, all-day north-facing sunshine and seriously impressive views.\r\n\r\nYou can hire a builder, but you can't buy orientation.\r\n\r\nReclad, renovate, or completely redesign - the potential here is massive for anyone with the vision to unlock it.\r\n\r\nBecause what you're really buying here is the stuff you can't change:\r\n\r\nThe freehold land.\r\nThe private position.\r\nThe sun.\r\nThe views.\r\nAnd a whole lot of potential.\r\n\r\nThe property is vacant and this one needs to be sold.\r\n\r\nBring the vision. Unlock the upside.",
